IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`

-- Expectations that are MEANT TO FAIL: each asserts the answer of a reading of the statute that the fork register
-- (NOTES.md section 3, entries F1 to F25) considered and rejected. The encoding takes the other reading, so every
-- assertion here must fail. check.sh counts them (expected_failed in check.sh, expected_red in encoding.json: 12),
-- and the file doubles as proof that this harness can fail. If one of them ever passes, the encoding has
-- changed its reading.

§ `Tests that are meant to fail: readings considered and rejected`

§§ `F1 (R3): s 10 counts the day it starts from`

-- Rejected: "from" a day includes the day, so three years from 2025-07-16 end the day before the anniversary.
-- s 10(a) says the day "לא יבוא במנין"; (b) puts the end on the day with the event's number.
#ASSERT (`s 10 — the last day of a period of` 3 `years from the day` (YMD 2025 7 16)) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 15

-- Rejected: thirty days from 2026-01-01 with 2026-01-01 counted as day 1.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30

§§ `F25: month and year arithmetic that rolls forward instead of stopping at the last day of the month`

-- Rejected: the lenient `Date` constructor's answer, 3 March, for one month after 31 January 2025.
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 3

-- Rejected: 1 March 2025 for one year after 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT (`s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 1 `years after an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1

§§ `F3: what s 10(c) does with several rest days in a row`

-- Rejected reading B: each rest day among the last days of the period is "not counted" and replaced by one more
-- day, so two rest days at the end (Fri 30, Sat 31 January 2026) push the end by two days, to Mon 2 February.
-- Taken: the period does not end on a rest day, so it ends on the first day that is not one, Sun 1 February.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 30), (YMD 2026 1 31)))) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 2

-- Rejected reading C: the rest days at the end fall out of the period, so it ends on the last day before them.
#ASSERT (`s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2026 1 31)))) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30

§§ `F2: s 10(c) reaches only periods in days and weeks`

-- Rejected: (c) speaks of counting days, so a period in months or years ends on its nominal day even if that is a rest day.
-- Taken: (c) says "ימי תקופה" (the days of a period) without limiting the kind of period.
#ASSERT (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 1 `months after an event on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (LIST (YMD 2025 2 28), (YMD 2025 3 1), (YMD 2025 3 2)))) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

§§ `F5 and F12: the closing midnight and the first minute`

-- Rejected: the closing midnight belongs only to the next day (the half-open reading), asserted of the reading
-- that takes s 3's "עד" with s 8.
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is within the day` (YMD 2026 3 1)

-- Rejected: a statute binds from midnight, the first moment of its day. s 21 says 00.01.
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `binds`

§§ `F4: s 8's "until" is exclusive`

-- Rejected: "until D" stops before D.
#ASSERT NOT `s 8 — the date` (YMD 2026 3 31) `is up to and including` (YMD 2026 3 31)

§§ `F16: Ordinance s 19 read with s 8`

-- Rejected: "no validity until the day of commencement" includes the day, so nothing made under the power is valid
-- on the commencement day itself. Taken: validity begins on the commencement day, since the section exists to
-- operate the enactment on that day.
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — the earliest day a regulation made under the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `may be valid, when it was needed to operate the enactment:` FALSE EQUALS `not before the day the enactment commences` (YMD 2026 7 2)

`a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` MEANS `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement` WITH
    `the day the enactment was given` IS YMD 2026 1 10
    `the day the enactment commences` IS YMD 2026 7 1
    `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day` IS TRUE
    `another intention is implied` IS FALSE

§§ `F17: "the majority of them" means at least half`

-- Rejected: two of four is "their majority". Taken: a majority is more than half.
#ASSERT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 4 `persons was validly done when` 2 `of them did it`
